<title>JAPAN: Haseko seen posting 1.8 bln yen H1 profit--paper.</title>
<headline>Haseko seen posting 1.8 bln yen H1 profit--paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Haseko Corp is seen posting a parent current profit of 1.8 billion yen in the six months to September 30, after suffering a loss in the same period a year ago, a Japanese newspaper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun said the company is expected to be favoured by a likely rapid decline in a defict in its real estate division, as well as unexpectedly large profits from its earlier share sales.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment on the report.</p>
</text>
